{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "06IL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F = \\underline{k[\\epsilon]}/G$", "MATH_0002": "$G \\subset \\text{Aut}_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}(k[\\epsilon])$", "MATH_0003": "$\\underline{k[\\epsilon]} \\to F$", "MATH_0004": "$F$", "MATH_0005": "$k$", "MATH_0006": "$k$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-bijective-orbits}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-do-not-get-S2}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e17c0b1e66a89ee51984a31f31b411895a593dae6127107a043125224f8a3dd5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:703c5d15ee837c657008c5760da5176012166af621590ddb85a8f3b2b030f538", "source_text": "There exist predeformation categories which have a versal formal\nobject satisfying (<REF_0001>) but which do not\nsatisfy (S2). A quick example is to take <MATH_0001>\nwhere <MATH_0002>\nis a finite nontrivial subgroup. Namely, the map\n<MATH_0003> is smooth, but the tangent space\nof <MATH_0004> does not have a natural <MATH_0005>-vector space structure (as it is\na quotient of a <MATH_0006>-vector space by a finite group).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ffe8b126461993d27b17537742e4a1ecee56ce6221d753d4e3332e490cd14e92", "unit_id": "tag:06T7:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06IL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-bijective-orbits}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-construct-bijective-orbits}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5407f3381e3c59fb1dafb63aa5ce9f34521fbfecefbfaecbd978d086d68efb5c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f3a8cc0826ba23261abc3ee2eec4ca67f962a8f0150964ad94da628a90e1298", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a predeformation category satisfying\n(S2) which has a versal formal object. Then its minimal versal\nformal object satisfies (<REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:feab502d34db03639c1ca872ff5c3cf3b1c3262e204ad4aa9dfb243aaff2b07f", "unit_id": "tag:06T8:statement"}
